a)	Explore Spring Framework modules (e.g., Core, Data Access, Web)
Aim: To explore and understand the core architectural modules of the Spring Framework (Core Container, Data Access/Integration, and Web) and document their respective roles and configurations.

Conceptual Overview of Key Modules:
•	Core Container: Consists of the Beans, Core, Context, and SpEL (Spring Expression Language) modules. It provides the fundamental IoC (Inversion of Control) and Dependency Injection features.
•	Data Access / Integration: Includes JDBC, ORM, OXM, JMS, and the Transaction modules. It simplifies database connectivity, manages transaction states, and reduces boilerplate SQL exception-handling code.
•	Web (MVC / WebFlux): Contains the Web, Web-Servlet (MVC), Web-Socket, and Web-Portlet modules. It implements the Model-View-Controller design pattern for building responsive, decoupled web applications.

